## Subagents

| Subagent | When |
|----------|------|
| **api-test-writer** | API endpoint coverage in `api/`; runs `--project=api` |
| **test-writer** | Page-flow plans → `tests/` (+ `pages/` when needed) |
| **triage** | Red run classification |
| **bug-reporter** | Confirmed product defects |

## Routing

After **jira-ticket-analyzer** (or **explore-and-generate** when there is no ticket), route by acceptance criteria:

| Plan shape | Delegation | Run |
|------------|------------|-----|
| API endpoint only (no page in AC) | [api-contract-tests](../skills/api-contract-tests/SKILL.md) from spec or [CATALOG.md](../../api/CATALOG.md) → **api-test-writer** | `npx playwright test --project=api` |
| Page flow | **test-writer** (read [pom-conventions](../skills/pom-conventions/SKILL.md) first) | `npx playwright test` (relevant `--project` / spec) |
| Both API and page | **api-test-writer** first, then **test-writer** | API project, then app specs |

**With ticket:** analyze → plan saved to `features/<key>.feature.md` → route per table → if red, **Heal on red**.

**No ticket:** explore-and-generate → plan saved to `features/explore-<slug>.feature.md` → route per table.

## Heal on red

Always **triage** first (P36 **evidence score** applies to API failures too — classify from trace, status, and body vs catalog/spec).

| Classification | Action |
|----------------|--------|
| Real app bug | **bug-reporter** — never heal |
| Drift (UI locator) | **self-heal**: re-discover via accessibility snapshot, patch POM only, re-run green with assertions unchanged, repair PR `heal/<desc>` — never merge |
| Ambiguous | Stop and escalate |

**API failures:** no page object to heal — the drift path cannot reach **act**. A changed status or response field is **not** self-heal; keep triage’s classification as evidence for a **contract change** (human updates catalog/spec and assertions) or a **bug** — never route to **self-heal**.

**Hard stops:** never touch an assertion (guard hooks enforce it); stop if green needs an assertion change or the same locator error persists.

## Backlog mode

The outer runner (Cursor Automation, headless `agent -p`, or local batch) queries Jira project `JIRA_PROJECT_KEY` (`AQPBT`) for status **In QA** without label `tests-generated` and passes **at most one** ticket per run. Empty queue → no run.

Per ticket: analyze → route (API and/or page writers) → run → heal on red.

**Output:** one PR per ticket, ticket linked in PR body, label `tests-generated` on the ticket — never merge, transition, or close.

**Stop on repeated identical failure:** leave PR open; do not add the label.

## Done

Apply [eval-report](../skills/eval-report/SKILL.md) when any trigger fired this session; commit refreshed `eval-report.md`. Otherwise note `eval: skipped`.

| Mode | Done when |
|------|-----------|
| **Single ticket** | Spec green locally (or repair PR open with human approval pending), plan in `features/`, eval handled |
| **Backlog** | One PR per processed ticket (or stopped per repeated failure), labels/links as above, eval handled |
| **Red-run heal** | Triage complete; drift → heal PR open green on re-run; bug → Jira key reported after human approval; eval handled |
